@{
}
<a class="govuk-back-link" href="javascript:window.history.back()">Back</a>

<div class="govuk-main-wrapper">
    <div class="govuk-grid-row">
    <div class="govuk-grid-column-two-thirds">
        <h1 class="govuk-heading-l">
            Connect to the Data Marketplace API
        </h1>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            This API allows you to automatically publish and update listings in
            the Data Marketplace’s catalogue, using information from your organisation’s data catalogue or data store.
        </p>
        <p class="govuk-body">
            You’ll need someone with technical expertise and knowledge of APIs
            to do this integration. Typically this will be an API developer.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            If you’re a developer, you can <a class="govuk-link" href="/support/support-api">get started with the API</a>.
        </p>

        <h2 class="govuk-heading-m">
            Ask your developer to join the Data Marketplace
        </h2>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            Your API developer must work in your organisation and have a government email address with your organisation’s
            domain (for example, hmrc.gov.uk).
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            They need to <a class="govuk-link" href="/support/get-started">create a Data Marketplace account</a> and then request the Metadata Publisher role from
            their user profile.
        </p>

        <p class="govuk-body">
            They will then be able to connect to the API.
        </p>

    </div>

    </div>
</div>